1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:07,000
(Q11（单选）) Welcome to this podcast about the Sheep market, which is one of the oldest parts of the city.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:20,001
[定位词 rapidly growing = fastest] As its name suggests, there was originally a market here where farmers brought their sheep, but now it's been redeveloped into a buzzing, vibrant area of the city, which is also home to one of the city's fastest-growing communities.

3
00:00:20,001 --> 00:00:26,044
[❌B， 偷换概念，这个地方只是popular with students，和是否fast-grow无关] The nearby university has always meant the area's popular with students, who come in to enjoy the lively nightlife,&nbsp;

4
00:00:26,044 --> 00:00:37,262
[Q11答案句  ✅A 解释型， embark on careers in ... fashion and design = professional] but now graduates embarking on careers in the worlds of fashion and design are buying up the new apartments recently built here to replace the small houses where the market workers used to live.

5
00:00:37,262 --> 00:00:47,652
(Q12) [Q12答案句   🟢 side streets原词；✅ great place 态度词出现， 符合题干recommend，注意听； ✅C =arts and crafts] The narrow old side streets are great places for finding original pictures, jewellery and ceramics which won't break the bank, as well as local produce like fruit and vegetables.

6
00:00:47,652 --> 00:00:53,807
[❌A， 偷换概念。 all over the world 是游客来自世界各地，跟restaurant是否international没关系] There's also lots of pavement cafes where you can have a coffee and watch tourists from all over the world go by.

7
00:00:53,807 --> 00:01:02,545
[❌B，偷换概念，1.只说了有个古老的建筑+一些事实，但没有态度词；2.还是在main street上的，不是side street] The oldest buildings in the area are on the main streets, including the city's first department store, built in the 1880s, which is still open today.

8
00:01:02,545 --> 00:01:09,102
(Q13) The Sheep market is a centre for fashion, and there's a policy of encouraging new young designers. Sheep market

9
00:01:09,102 --> 00:01:14,867
[🟢定位词 专有名词 YFC] The Young Fashion competition is open to local young people who are passionate about fashion.

10
00:01:14,867 --> 00:01:20,789
[Q13答案句 be asked to= must ， ✅B： idea from music & tech ... everyday life = contemporary culture] This year they've been asked to design an outfit based on the ideas from the music and technology that's part of their everyday life,&nbsp;

11
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:24,367
[❌C， 断章取义， 仅说到天然&人造fibres， locally没提到] using both natural and man-made fibres.

12
00:01:24,367 --> 00:01:31,534
[❌A没提及， 听到model，只是说入围作品会被展出，没说被谁展出] The garments will be judged by a panel of experts and fashion designers, and the winning entries will be modelled at a special gala evening.

13
00:01:31,534 --> 00:01:45,099
(Q14) [🟢 上来就是定位词 park； ❌A，否定原文， 说了要收费 pay and display] Parking at the Sheep market is easy. There are plenty of pay and display car parking spaces on the roadsides which are fine if you just want to stay for an hour or two（选项A）, but if you want to spend the day there it's better to park in one of the for underground carparks.

14
00:01:45,099 --> 00:01:51,370
[Q12答案句 ✅B， receipts from 当地商店= buy，解释型； won't be charged at all = free 解释型] It's not expensive and if you can present a receipt from one of the local stores, you'll not be charged at all.

15
00:01:51,370 --> 00:01:57,533
[❌C， after 6pm= in the evening；  rate 费率 否定原文，要收费的] After six pm many of the car parks have a flat rate which varies but it is usually very reasonable.

16
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:02,647
(Q15（地图🗺️）) The Sheep market is one of the main centres for art and history in the whole of the country. Sheep market

17
00:02:02,647 --> 00:02:10,383
If you look at our map, you'll see some of the main attractions there. Most visitors start from Crawley Road, at the bottom of the map.

18
00:02:10,383 --> 00:02:15,693
The Reynolds House is one of the oldest houses in the city, and is open to the public. Reynolds House

19
00:02:15,693 --> 00:02:21,854
It's on the north side of Crawley Road, next to the footpath that leads to the public gardens.

20
00:02:21,854 --> 00:02:35,068
(Q16) The area's particularly interesting for its unusual sculptures. 'The Thumb' is just what its name suggests, but it's about 10 metres high. You'll see it on Hill Road, across the road from the Bank.

21
00:02:35,068 --> 00:02:39,622
(Q17) The Museum's got a particularly fine collection of New Zealand landscapes.

22
00:02:39,622 --> 00:02:49,889
It's on the east side of the Sheep market, on City Road. It's on the other side of the road from the public gardens, immediately facing the junction with Hill Road.

23
00:02:49,889 --> 00:02:56,935
(Q18) The Contemporary Art Gallery is on a little road that leads off Station Square, not far from the public gardens.

24
00:02:56,935 --> 00:03:03,377
The road ends at the gallery - it doesn't go anywhere else. That's open every day except Mondays.

25
00:03:03,377 --> 00:03:14,383
(Q19) The Warner Gallery specialises in 19th-century art. It's on City Road, near the junction with Crawley Road, on the same side of the road as the public gardens. Warner

26
00:03:14,383 --> 00:03:19,281
It's open on weekdays from 9 to 5, and entry is free.

27
00:03:19,281 --> 00:03:26,520
(Q20) Finally, if you're interested in purchasing high quality artwork, the place to go is Nucleus. Warner

28
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:35,550
You need to go from Crawley Road up through Station Square and east along Hill Road until you get to a small winding road turning off.

29
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:38,050
Go up there and it's on your right - if you get to City Road you've gone too far.

